{"name":"Tricorn Black","hex":"#2f2f30","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tricorn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A three-cornered hat, with the brim turned up.","A three-horned fractal."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having three horns or similar projections."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tricorn"},{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tricorne","blocks":[{"text":"The tricorne or tricorn is a style of hat in a triangular shape, which became popular in Europe during the 18th century, falling out of style by the early 1800s. The word \"tricorne\" was not widely used until the mid-19th century. During the 18th century, hats of this general style were referred to as \"cocked hats\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Tricorne_MET_DP-642-001.jpg/330px-Tricorne_MET_DP-642-001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tricorne"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Mousquetaires-de-la-maison-du-roi-.jpg/330px-Mousquetaires-de-la-maison-du-roi-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Mousquetaires-de-la-maison-du-roi-.jpg/330px-Mousquetaires-de-la-maison-du-roi-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"French Musketeers of the Guard wearing tricorne hats in 1688","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMousquetaires-de-la-maison-du-roi-.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Alabardero.JPG/120px-Alabardero.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Alabardero.JPG/250px-Alabardero.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Alabardero.JPG/120px-Alabardero.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlabardero.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Guardia_Civil_a_caballo_Dos_de_Mayo_2008_n5.jpg/120px-Guardia_Civil_a_caballo_Dos_de_Mayo_2008_n5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Guardia_Civil_a_caballo_Dos_de_Mayo_2008_n5.jpg/250px-Guardia_Civil_a_caballo_Dos_de_Mayo_2008_n5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Guardia_Civil_a_caballo_Dos_de_Mayo_2008_n5.jpg/120px-Guardia_Civil_a_ca